<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kumma</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kumma was an Egyptian fortress of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Kingdom</a> on the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semna">Semna</a> gorge, south of the Second Cataract in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-nubia">Lower Nubia</a>, facing the fortress of Semna on the west bank. Built under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senusret-iii">Senusret III</a>, it helped guard <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s southern frontier. Its temple was moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khartoum">Khartoum</a> before the site was flooded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-nasser">Lake Nasser</a>.</p></div>
